<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-UHIS TO GET 12 MLN DM CREDIT LINE.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-UHIS TO GET 12 MLN DM CREDIT LINE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uhispank said on Tuesday it will receive a 12 million German mark housing finance facility with a 10-year maturity from the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD).</p>
<p>The interest rate of the loan will be mark LIBOR plus a marginal, Janek Maggi, Uhispank vice-president, told Reuters.  </p>
<p>EBRD has passed an initial review of the project and the board will discuss the loan facility on July 1.</p>
<p>Uhispank is the second-largest bank in Estonia and is listed on the stock exchanges of Tallinn and Helsinki and traded on the Munich bourse.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 6 209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
